  "user": "Fine. Back to that charge — what do I do next?",
  "answer": "I've checked the account (ACC-1005) and the two TechMart Online card charges. Nothing has been filed.\n\n**The two charges:**\n- **TX-0402**, 14 July 2026, €240.00, TechMart Online, settled\n- **TX-0401**, 20 July 2026, €240.00, TechMart Online, settled\n\n**Eligibility for a duplicate-charge dispute:**\n- **TX-0401 (20 July): eligible.** The deadline is **18 September 2026**, so you have a few days.\n- **TX-0402 (14 July): not eligible.** Its 60-day window closed on 12 September 2026.\n\nBefore I open anything, I need you to confirm:\n1. Is the duplicate charge TX-0401 (20 July, €240.00)? Opening a dispute is irreversible, so I want the right transaction.\n2. Is the duplicate-charge reason correct? That means you were billed twice for the same purchase. If instead you paid for something you never received or that wasn't delivered as described, the reason would be different (service not rendered or goods not received), and I would check eligibility for that code first.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll run the eligibility check for the reason you choose and, if it passes, open the dispute.",
